			"Message": "build(deps): bump pnpm/action-setup from 5.0.0 to 6.0.0\n\nBumps [pnpm/action-setup](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup) from 5.0.0 to 6.0.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/compare/v5.0.0...v6.0.0)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: pnpm/action-setup\n  dependency-version: 6.0.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "29a644774f16762432ef98f2bd0527f404051ca6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T21:36:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				76,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add VS Code terminal and language detection node_modules\n\nAdd @xterm/xterm with all addon packages and @vscode/vscode-languagedetection to dependencies. Update the astro.config.ts build step to copy these node_modules to Static/Application/node_modules/ for runtime access.\n\nThese packages are required for VS Code's terminal emulation and language detection functionality, enabling the editor to provide full VS Code feature parity.",
			"SHA": "56196122900e982b16cc67236237c6f4c863c2ef"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T21:27:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				76,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Expand Blob patch to rewrite vscode-file:// URLs and simplify polyfill comments\n\nRefactor the Blob constructor patch in Workbench.ts to handle VS Code worker file URLs more robustly:\n\n1. Remove the restrictive `_VSCODE_NLS_MESSAGES` check — now applies the __name shim to all application/javascript blobs for broader compatibility\n2. Add URL rewriting: convert `vscode-file://vscode-app/Static/Application/out/` paths to `${origin}/Static/Application/` so Tauri can serve VS Code assets locally\n3. Simplify the three separate WKWebView polyfill comments into a single grouped comment\n\nThis ensures VS Code extension workers can load assets correctly in Tauri's webview environment.",
			"SHA": "4f5bc5e2192fa23f1365fda5fb951ce4f4361055"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T13:29:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				76,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add VS Code CDN and file scheme CSP permissions\n\nAdd Content Security Policy permissions required for VS Code extension host and webview functionality:\n1. frame-src: Allow vscode-webview.net, *.vscode-cdn.net, *.vscode-webview.net for extension iframe loading\n2. script-src/style-src/connect-src: Allow vscode-file: and vscode-file://vscode-app for local file access in extensions\n3. connect-src: Allow blob: and ipc: for extension host communication\n\nAdditionally, implement a Blob constructor patch in Workbench.ts that intercepts VS Code worker bootstrap blobs and injects the __name shim. This ensures extension host blob workers have access to esbuild's __name helper without requiring external fetches.\n\nThese changes enable VS Code extensions to load properly from CDN sources and access local file resources.",
			"SHA": "736ca262610b3babbbb82e86b8b2b5fdb6138d89"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T09:55:45Z",
